      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should change this log line.  It\u0027s matched to the one on line 283, and the new text is misleading.  This is a single \"Upload job\", which launches X \"Endpoint upload jobs\".  The endpoint upload jobs are handled below, and they have their own matching log lines for \"Starting upload X\" and \"Finished upload X\" (I think it\u0027d be okay to change those to \"endpoint upload\", but they\u0027re still at least distinct from what we have here).\n\nYou\u0027re adding the extra information of how many endpoint upload jobs were processed -- that is currently available by counting the log lines from the endpoint upload jobs, but that\u0027s not convenient.\n\nI think we can add that here if you want, but let\u0027s just try to be precise in the phrasing.  So maybe:\n\n\"Finished upload job for %s with %s uploads.\"  or \"Finished upload job for %s with %s endpoint uploads.\"",
