      "side": 1,
      "message": "We rarely set timeouts for things like this -- can you elaborate on your reasoning here?  Because my understanding is that this is called after the completion of validation jobs, which would only be triggered after the upload, so there should be nothing in contention with this (except as you note, the case where everything is really fast and the pipeline somehow completes between lines 356 and 362 of the launcher server -- which are basically two immediately successive instructions, so with the rest of this change, that seems really unlikely).  I suspect you were more likely to observe this issue with the *old* code (which held the lock longer) than the new code which releases locks immediately.\n\nI guess my worry is that with a 30 second timeout, we\u0027re more likely to hit that due to a very slow scheduler or zookeeper, or perhaps a zookeeper connectivity issue rather than any actual contention.\n\nI think our normal expectation would be not to have a timeout here.  We didn\u0027t before, and we also don\u0027t on the IBA.  I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary, and I think in the case where we somehow manage to not acquire the lock for 30s due to system slowness, having the scheduler wait is probably good.\n\nIf you would like to change our practice and start to add timeouts for unexpected situations, maybe it should be very long?  Like 3-5 minutes rather than 30 seconds?\n\nI prefer no timeout, but if you feel strongly about adding them, then I\u0027d like longer ones and also we should add it to the IBA in the method above this one.",
